1
00:00:10,345 --> 00:00:11,185
Jump down!

2
00:00:12,625 --> 00:00:13,625
Woohoo!

3
00:00:14,265 --> 00:00:16,625
Finally, it’s shower time! I stink.

4
00:00:16,865 --> 00:00:17,705
Yay!

5
00:00:18,465 --> 00:00:19,305
I'm scared.

6
00:00:20,305 --> 00:00:21,505
Hurry up. Jump!

7
00:00:21,705 --> 00:00:22,745
Get on, Dum.

8
00:00:22,745 --> 00:00:24,345
Jump in. What are you afraid of ?

9
00:00:25,105 --> 00:00:27,065
Jump down. Jump.

10
00:00:32,385 --> 00:00:33,825
Hey! got it.

11
00:00:36,425 --> 00:00:37,865
Where's my sarong?

12
00:00:37,865 --> 00:00:38,865
What's the sarong?

13
00:00:39,465 --> 00:00:40,105
Sarong...

14
00:00:40,105 --> 00:00:40,745
What?

15
00:00:41,465 --> 00:00:42,025
Where's it?

16
00:00:42,025 --> 00:00:42,865
Do you want this?

17
00:00:44,225 --> 00:00:46,225
Asshole! Give me my sarong back.

18
00:00:46,745 --> 00:00:51,185
Give me my sarong back.

19
00:00:54,105 --> 00:00:56,305
This is not a playground.

20
00:00:57,465 --> 00:00:59,265
If your noise drowns out the alarm,

21
00:00:59,745 --> 00:01:01,025
you won’t escape in time.

22
00:01:02,025 --> 00:01:04,265
Especially you, the loudest one.

23
00:01:06,625 --> 00:01:09,105
Let's finish the shower, so you can have a meal then.

24
00:01:13,385 --> 00:01:13,985
Give me!

25
00:01:13,985 --> 00:01:16,225
Everyone's at it so why the hell is he scolding me alone?

26
00:01:16,465 --> 00:01:18,945
You swear again, Comrade Saeng.

27
00:01:18,945 --> 00:01:20,985
They just told us not to swear.

28
00:01:20,985 --> 00:01:22,065
You're gonna get it again.

29
00:02:16,345 --> 00:02:18,825
What are you doing? Why don't you go take a shower?

30
00:02:18,825 --> 00:02:20,865
It's getting dark early out here, unlike in the city.

31
00:02:22,025 --> 00:02:22,545
Yes, sir.

32
00:02:27,945 --> 00:02:28,665
So strict!

33
00:02:34,705 --> 00:02:36,225
Yes, I'm coming.

34
00:02:37,705 --> 00:02:38,545
Hey!

35
00:02:41,465 --> 00:02:44,105
Aren’t you going to take a shower, Comrade Ying?

36
00:02:44,385 --> 00:02:45,785
You'll miss your meal.

37
00:02:46,985 --> 00:02:49,425
I'll do it after putting my things away.

38
00:02:49,425 --> 00:02:51,665
What's your name, sis?

39
00:02:52,345 --> 00:02:55,025
Dad said everyone is equal here.

40
00:02:55,025 --> 00:02:56,865
You can call me Comrade Bai Tong.

41
00:02:57,265 --> 00:02:59,145
Sure, Comrade Bai Tong.

42
00:03:00,665 --> 00:03:05,345
Comrade Bai tong, do you know.. a sanitary pad?

43
00:03:06,505 --> 00:03:07,625
What's the pad?

44
00:03:09,745 --> 00:03:13,905
A sanitary pad is a pad used to absorb menstrual blood.

45
00:03:17,185 --> 00:03:20,385
Never mind, I'll ask Comrade Roong.

46
00:03:20,985 --> 00:03:23,225
So, if you're free,

47
00:03:23,225 --> 00:03:25,505
could you tell me about the world outside?

48
00:03:26,425 --> 00:03:30,225
Sure, you can ask me anything you want to know

49
00:03:30,745 --> 00:03:32,145
Yay!

50
00:03:32,465 --> 00:03:33,425
Let's take a shower.

51
00:03:36,225 --> 00:03:39,465
I'll tell you. Do you know Thai Daimaru?

52
00:03:39,465 --> 00:03:40,665
It's a department store, it has everything.

53
00:03:48,305 --> 00:03:49,585
Is it edible?

54
00:03:50,065 --> 00:03:54,185
Sure. It’s a blessing to find some food in the forest.

55
00:03:55,585 --> 00:03:56,905
How do I eat this?

56
00:03:57,585 --> 00:04:00,305
We eat to live, not live to eat.

57
00:04:02,505 --> 00:04:03,865
That hits hard, comrade.

58
00:04:04,545 --> 00:04:05,545
Next.

59
00:04:06,065 --> 00:04:07,065
Thanks.

60
00:04:10,385 --> 00:04:10,985
Are you alright?

61
00:04:11,145 --> 00:04:12,105
Comrade Meut

62
00:04:12,145 --> 00:04:12,705
Huh?

63
00:04:13,385 --> 00:04:14,705
I think we should stay away from Comrade Saeng.

64
00:04:15,345 --> 00:04:15,985
Why?

65
00:04:16,745 --> 00:04:18,185
Or else we'll all be in trouble too.

66
00:04:18,825 --> 00:04:19,465
There's a point.

67
00:04:20,665 --> 00:04:21,665
So much for being a team.

68
00:04:37,665 --> 00:04:38,345
Mada..

69
00:04:40,345 --> 00:04:41,545
Why do you come late?

70
00:04:43,185 --> 00:04:44,105
I feel a little stomachache.

71
00:04:46,105 --> 00:04:47,025
Go grab a plate.

72
00:04:49,345 --> 00:04:51,825
it's kinda like porridge, I guess.

73
00:04:52,145 --> 00:04:55,065
This is Comrade Saeng.

74
00:04:55,545 --> 00:04:57,785
This is Comrade Bai Tong, a daughter of Comrade Ploeng.

75
00:04:58,545 --> 00:05:01,185
Comrade Bai Tong, can I change the menu next time?

76
00:05:01,505 --> 00:05:03,585
Eating porridge and yams is unbearable.

77
00:05:03,585 --> 00:05:06,665
Sure, then eat a boiled yams and porridge tomorrow.

78
00:05:07,145 --> 00:05:08,625
What's the difference?

79
00:05:08,825 --> 00:05:10,785
We eat to live, not live to eat.

80
00:05:11,665 --> 00:05:13,145
That line again!

81
00:05:17,865 --> 00:05:18,705
Deal with it.

82
00:05:20,465 --> 00:05:22,585
You'll get used to it, if you eat often.

83
00:05:34,625 --> 00:05:36,785
My dear comrades.

84
00:05:39,265 --> 00:05:42,145
Our goal and ideology

85
00:05:42,145 --> 00:05:45,425
are not only fighting against the government,

86
00:05:46,905 --> 00:05:50,145
but we fight against the injustice,

87
00:05:50,385 --> 00:05:51,625
and the inequality.

88
00:05:51,625 --> 00:05:53,305
We also fight against the poverty

89
00:05:53,305 --> 00:05:55,185
that oppresses the people in the upcountry.

90
00:05:55,345 --> 00:05:57,305
To all of my beloved comrades,

91
00:05:57,905 --> 00:06:00,865
I want you to learn everything

92
00:06:00,865 --> 00:06:03,185
from our base as much as possible.

93
00:06:03,385 --> 00:06:05,705
So all of you can become the main force...

94
00:06:06,225 --> 00:06:09,025
to improve our country.

95
00:06:09,425 --> 00:06:13,265
Male comrades, while you’re here,

96
00:06:13,465 --> 00:06:17,305
if you have any questions, please ask Comrade Yue.

97
00:06:20,145 --> 00:06:23,745
Female comrades, please ask Comrade Roong.

98
00:06:24,025 --> 00:06:29,025
A topic like a romance - who loves whom.

99
00:06:29,025 --> 00:06:32,265
must report to the responsible comrade.

100
00:06:32,985 --> 00:06:34,985
Me and Comrade Ying, we're dating.

101
00:06:37,665 --> 00:06:39,625
Dating? What is this?

102
00:06:40,945 --> 00:06:42,625
It means we are lovers

103
00:06:46,825 --> 00:06:48,945
Why do we have to report who loves whom?

104
00:06:50,025 --> 00:06:52,305
So the leader knows,

105
00:06:52,305 --> 00:06:54,665
and can help resolve any issues.

106
00:06:54,865 --> 00:06:55,945
When two people are in love..

107
00:06:55,945 --> 00:06:57,585
why do we need anyone else to handle this?

108
00:06:57,585 --> 00:06:59,505
Don't interrupt while Comrade Ploeng is speaking.

109
00:07:00,665 --> 00:07:02,825
I'm not, I already raised my hand first.

110
00:07:03,265 --> 00:07:06,265
It's OK, go ahead and ask.

111
00:07:08,385 --> 00:07:09,745
That kid is mischievous.

112
00:07:18,625 --> 00:07:21,065
Does anybody know about The Three Delays Policy?

113
00:07:21,105 --> 00:07:22,825
I do.

114
00:07:23,065 --> 00:07:24,905
The Three Delays Policy is delayed love,

115
00:07:24,905 --> 00:07:26,505
delayed marriage, delayed childbirth.

116
00:07:26,705 --> 00:07:28,585
Love causes chaos.

117
00:07:28,585 --> 00:07:30,585
The Party wants everyone to focus on their work

118
00:07:30,585 --> 00:07:32,465
and devote themselves to the mission first.

119
00:07:32,745 --> 00:07:34,145
He already knows.

120
00:07:34,145 --> 00:07:36,305
That's it, why does he need to tell that he has a girlfirend?

121
00:07:36,665 --> 00:07:37,745
Yeah, that's right.

122
00:07:37,745 --> 00:07:40,305
Good. Sit down.

123
00:07:41,705 --> 00:07:46,825
Tonight please take a full rest, dismissed.

124
00:08:07,065 --> 00:08:09,225
I get what The Three Delays Policy is.

125
00:08:09,225 --> 00:08:11,745
But the feeling is hard to resist.

126
00:08:12,345 --> 00:08:13,585
They don’t forbid it,

127
00:08:13,905 --> 00:08:16,305
they just want to slow things down.

128
00:08:17,505 --> 00:08:19,865
Nobody can resist it forever.

129
00:08:20,985 --> 00:08:23,145
They say there’s no rule here,

130
00:08:23,465 --> 00:08:25,105
but in the end, there’s still a restriction

131
00:08:25,665 --> 00:08:27,665
That’s what happens when you have to manage a lot of people.

132
00:08:27,665 --> 00:08:29,705
Every place needs rules to control people.

133
00:08:30,905 --> 00:08:32,945
Got it, but I don’t accept it.

134
00:08:35,265 --> 00:08:37,465
You oppose The Three Delays Policy,

135
00:08:37,465 --> 00:08:39,625
as if you're in love with someone.

136
00:08:40,065 --> 00:08:41,105
Are you seeing someone?

137
00:08:41,105 --> 00:08:43,065
Are you?

138
00:08:43,145 --> 00:08:43,625
Tell us.

139
00:08:43,625 --> 00:08:46,945
No, no, no, not yet.

140
00:08:47,745 --> 00:08:51,785
I wanna know who can stir comrade Sang’s heart.

141
00:08:51,785 --> 00:08:53,745
Who will it be?

142
00:08:53,745 --> 00:08:56,505
Anyone who makes me feel comfortable.

143
00:08:57,505 --> 00:09:00,025
But now we should focus on our goal, right?

144
00:09:00,065 --> 00:09:02,225
How to make our country better.

145
00:09:02,225 --> 00:09:03,665
That's all.

146
00:09:05,585 --> 00:09:07,065
Three of us,

147
00:09:07,265 --> 00:09:08,705
will make it happen.

148
00:09:09,545 --> 00:09:10,825
Deal?

149
00:09:10,865 --> 00:09:12,185
Deal.

150
00:09:13,105 --> 00:09:14,465
Great.

151
00:09:16,945 --> 00:09:18,265
I don't like Comrade Saeng.

152
00:09:19,185 --> 00:09:20,505
He’s been mouthing off since he got here.

153
00:09:24,345 --> 00:09:25,585
You haven’t even known him for a day.

154
00:09:26,185 --> 00:09:27,425
You’re already judging him?

155
00:09:31,785 --> 00:09:33,025
You're protecting him, right?

156
00:09:38,545 --> 00:09:39,785
It's a fact.

157
00:09:43,465 --> 00:09:44,705
Do you know ?

158
00:09:45,145 --> 00:09:47,945
that Comrade Saeng has the same last name as that cop?

159
00:09:54,745 --> 00:09:56,345
Too bad,

160
00:09:56,345 --> 00:09:58,025
The studen information has been kept with Comrade Ploeng.

161
00:09:59,545 --> 00:10:00,985
Otherwise, we will know it right away.

162
00:10:00,985 --> 00:10:01,985
So there’s no need to keep wondering.

163
00:10:07,345 --> 00:10:08,625
I guess not.

164
00:10:11,625 --> 00:10:13,545
This guy doesn't look like a bad cop.

165
00:11:41,425 --> 00:11:42,705
Dad!

166
00:12:02,785 --> 00:12:04,585
I'd better go. See you at the courtyard.

167
00:12:05,385 --> 00:12:06,785
Come quickly.

168
00:12:06,785 --> 00:12:08,225
OK. I'll catch up with you.

169
00:12:10,505 --> 00:12:12,545
Oh! Good morning, Comrade Yue.

170
00:12:12,545 --> 00:12:13,905
Hello, Comrade Yue.

171
00:12:16,665 --> 00:12:18,105
Wake up, Comrade Saeng!

172
00:12:18,105 --> 00:12:20,025
Hmm...just a minute.

173
00:12:20,185 --> 00:12:21,305
Please hurry.

174
00:12:21,625 --> 00:12:22,545
Yeah!

175
00:12:23,025 --> 00:12:23,945
Hello, Comrade.

176
00:12:29,665 --> 00:12:30,545
Comrade Saeng.

177
00:12:38,265 --> 00:12:39,065
Ahem!

178
00:12:39,665 --> 00:12:40,465
Comrade Saeng.

179
00:12:41,025 --> 00:12:42,465
Give me two secs.

180
00:12:48,105 --> 00:12:48,945
So drowsy!

181
00:13:31,385 --> 00:13:32,585
Stop being drowsy

182
00:13:33,785 --> 00:13:35,745
Do you want all the comrades at the base to wait for you?

183
00:13:47,345 --> 00:13:51,945
Shit! Is it the end of the world, Just woke up late.

184
00:13:52,585 --> 00:13:53,505
I hear you.

185
00:13:58,025 --> 00:13:59,985
Good, Comrade Yue.

186
00:14:00,425 --> 00:14:02,105
I'm coming now.

187
00:14:12,865 --> 00:14:14,105
Well, comrades,

188
00:14:14,825 --> 00:14:17,065
It's time to get your bodies strong.

189
00:14:17,745 --> 00:14:21,585
Brace yourselves to join a grand mission together.

190
00:14:21,705 --> 00:14:23,705
Ready? Repeat after me:

191
00:14:24,585 --> 00:14:30,225
Waist, shoulder, head, shoulder, waist.

192
00:14:31,105 --> 00:14:32,105
After walking this far,

193
00:14:32,105 --> 00:14:33,505
we still have to do this.

194
00:14:35,665 --> 00:14:38,865
If we are strong, and tough,

195
00:14:38,865 --> 00:14:41,945
we will have a strength to fight the opponent.

196
00:14:41,945 --> 00:14:42,585
Come on!

197
00:14:42,825 --> 00:14:44,065
Ho! Hey!

198
00:14:44,065 --> 00:14:44,865
How does he hear it?

199
00:14:44,865 --> 00:14:52,305
Ho! Hey! Ho! Hey!

200
00:14:52,305 --> 00:14:54,065
Louder! Yes!

201
00:14:54,065 --> 00:14:55,665
You're standing still though, Comrade Yue.

202
00:14:57,025 --> 00:14:59,145
You're standing still though, Comrade Yue.

203
00:15:00,745 --> 00:15:01,985
Switch to another exercise.

204
00:15:01,985 --> 00:15:03,265
Arm circles.

205
00:15:04,545 --> 00:15:05,825
Arm circles.

206
00:15:06,505 --> 00:15:07,785
Arm circles.

207
00:15:08,225 --> 00:15:09,505
Arm circles.

208
00:15:14,065 --> 00:15:15,345
Remember to shout Hey!

209
00:15:15,545 --> 00:15:16,625
Hey! Hey!

210
00:15:17,185 --> 00:15:18,265
Hey! Hey!

211
00:15:19,065 --> 00:15:20,305
เปลี่ยนท่า

212
00:15:20,305 --> 00:15:20,905
Everybody

213
00:15:20,905 --> 00:15:22,785
Time to backbend.

214
00:15:23,825 --> 00:15:24,745
Get in pair.

215
00:15:25,225 --> 00:15:25,585
Look.

216
00:15:25,585 --> 00:15:26,145
Urgh!

217
00:15:26,225 --> 00:15:27,665
Urgh!

218
00:15:27,665 --> 00:15:29,425
Like this.

219
00:15:29,665 --> 00:15:30,945
Urgh!

220
00:15:30,945 --> 00:15:36,425
Urgh!

221
00:15:37,345 --> 00:15:38,545
Comrade Yue.

222
00:15:38,625 --> 00:15:40,705
Help Comrade Saeng adjust his posture.

223
00:15:41,585 --> 00:15:42,345
Quick!

224
00:15:48,945 --> 00:15:51,065
Ouch!

225
00:15:53,145 --> 00:15:58,145
Argh!

226
00:16:00,945 --> 00:16:02,585
The newcomer students,

227
00:16:02,585 --> 00:16:04,305
they are a good force...

228
00:16:04,785 --> 00:16:06,385
to improve our troop.

229
00:16:06,385 --> 00:16:07,585
Make us stronger.

230
00:16:08,145 --> 00:16:09,625
We have to categorize them

231
00:16:09,625 --> 00:16:12,825
by their knowledge and abilities.

232
00:16:16,025 --> 00:16:19,065
Comrade Gaun Hin joined a group with Comrade Saeng.

233
00:16:19,065 --> 00:16:21,265
He was a university's leader

234
00:16:21,385 --> 00:16:24,585
He has a fair amount of knowledge in administration.

235
00:16:25,225 --> 00:16:26,785
If he works with the masses,

236
00:16:26,785 --> 00:16:29,185
He could become one of our key people.

237
00:16:29,705 --> 00:16:33,265
Send Comrade Guan Hin to the Political Unit.

238
00:16:33,265 --> 00:16:35,025
Working with masses

239
00:16:35,385 --> 00:16:37,065
can help him understand the villagers,

240
00:16:37,065 --> 00:16:39,345
so he can persuade them to join our movement.

241
00:16:41,065 --> 00:16:45,385
From what I’ve seen in her background,

242
00:16:45,625 --> 00:16:47,905
Comrade Ying studied education.

243
00:16:48,625 --> 00:16:51,625
Should we send her to the Education Unit?

244
00:16:51,625 --> 00:16:53,025
Comrade Ying is a calm person.

245
00:16:53,025 --> 00:16:55,785
But we're short-staffed at the Medical Unit right now.

246
00:16:57,025 --> 00:16:58,025
Good.

247
00:16:58,305 --> 00:16:59,305
So,

248
00:16:59,945 --> 00:17:03,425
Let Comrade Ying use her medical knowledge

249
00:17:03,425 --> 00:17:05,705
to persuade the masses to join us too.

250
00:17:08,825 --> 00:17:09,825
What about Comrade Saeng?

251
00:17:10,785 --> 00:17:12,785
He's a stubborn, hard to control.

252
00:17:13,025 --> 00:17:14,465
He could cause trouble for us.

253
00:17:14,505 --> 00:17:16,385
We shouldn't let him do an important task.

254
00:17:17,145 --> 00:17:18,585
But if we listen to his opinion,

255
00:17:19,345 --> 00:17:21,305
we could gain a new perspective on work.

256
00:17:21,585 --> 00:17:22,585
A weird perspective, I guess.

257
00:17:23,465 --> 00:17:24,345
Always breaking every rule.

258
00:17:25,225 --> 00:17:26,065
No

259
00:17:26,665 --> 00:17:28,785
Relax, Comrade Fah.

260
00:17:31,105 --> 00:17:33,345
All hits, Comrade!

261
00:17:36,945 --> 00:17:39,745
The person who dares to think and question,

262
00:17:40,265 --> 00:17:43,665
and knows their way around weapons, is interesting.

263
00:17:45,985 --> 00:17:48,185
If we train him some more,

264
00:17:48,185 --> 00:17:50,425
he could be our new leader in the future.

265
00:17:52,785 --> 00:17:55,905
Well, let's send Comrade Saeng to the Military Unit.

266
00:17:56,305 --> 00:17:57,705
He will be able to train both physically

267
00:17:58,065 --> 00:18:01,665
and in communication and mission planning.

268
00:18:02,945 --> 00:18:04,105
Yes, sir.

269
00:18:11,345 --> 00:18:12,465
If you'll excuse me.

270
00:18:23,945 --> 00:18:26,265
It has been a month since the student crackdown,

271
00:18:28,025 --> 00:18:31,145
but the domestic communist forces are growing stronger.

272
00:18:31,145 --> 00:18:33,625
Especially the students who fled into the forests

273
00:18:34,025 --> 00:18:35,865
they've become key allies.

274
00:18:36,465 --> 00:18:38,505
They use a “forest surrounding the city” strategy,

275
00:18:38,825 --> 00:18:40,465
set up bases in the upcountry,

276
00:18:40,465 --> 00:18:42,105
and stir villagers against the state.

277
00:18:43,065 --> 00:18:45,265
We can't let it go on.

278
00:18:45,665 --> 00:18:48,225
Our mission is to wipe them out as soon as possible.

279
00:18:58,505 --> 00:19:00,185
Dan.

280
00:19:03,145 --> 00:19:06,225
The student leaders that you asked me to search for,

281
00:19:07,625 --> 00:19:09,065
Have you heard anything?

282
00:19:09,065 --> 00:19:11,345
My team member said they're at northern region.

283
00:19:12,985 --> 00:19:14,505
Just because I’m keeping track of the situation,

284
00:19:14,505 --> 00:19:17,545
it doesn’t mean I agree with those kids.

285
00:19:20,585 --> 00:19:22,145
Dad, Vin and those students,

286
00:19:22,145 --> 00:19:23,585
they are not criminals.

287
00:19:23,585 --> 00:19:25,505
But they are on the other side.

288
00:19:25,505 --> 00:19:27,585
You should be aware of your own standpoint too.

289
00:19:59,145 --> 00:20:00,945
Your aim has improved a lot.

290
00:20:02,785 --> 00:20:04,945
I have a talent. It's a piece of cake, bro.

291
00:20:26,785 --> 00:20:28,345
Stop shooting, Comrades.

292
00:20:29,665 --> 00:20:31,105
Comrade Ploeng.

293
00:20:32,345 --> 00:20:33,385
What’s going on?

294
00:20:33,385 --> 00:20:35,185
There's news from the main base.

295
00:20:49,865 --> 00:20:52,505
Comrade Ploeng, you can handle it.

296
00:20:52,905 --> 00:20:55,185
Comrades, please continue training. I'll take care of it.

297
00:20:57,705 --> 00:21:01,465
The main base commands us to send all new comrades...

298
00:21:01,545 --> 00:21:03,345
recruit more of the masses.

299
00:21:04,585 --> 00:21:06,985
Comrade Phu Pha, please inform Comrade Yaguar.

300
00:21:07,425 --> 00:21:10,585
Prepare to lead all new comrades into the village.

301
00:21:11,185 --> 00:21:12,465
Yes, sir.

302
00:21:12,465 --> 00:21:13,585
Comrade Yue,

303
00:21:13,985 --> 00:21:17,145
I want you to train Comrade Saeng in shooting a bit more.

304
00:21:17,545 --> 00:21:19,145
He is very promising.

305
00:21:19,545 --> 00:21:20,745
Sure, Comrade Ploeng.

306
00:21:21,985 --> 00:21:22,825
Letting a newbie

307
00:21:22,825 --> 00:21:23,665
join the army...

308
00:21:24,105 --> 00:21:25,505
without knowing his background.

309
00:21:25,505 --> 00:21:26,585
I think it's too risky.

310
00:21:26,945 --> 00:21:28,305
I've already checked.

311
00:21:28,825 --> 00:21:30,465
His profile is clean.

312
00:21:31,705 --> 00:21:34,025
We have the talented kid in our base,

313
00:21:34,585 --> 00:21:36,945
we must use his abilities to our advantage.

314
00:21:37,945 --> 00:21:39,385
In the future,

315
00:21:39,385 --> 00:21:42,705
he could become a new main force for our base.

316
00:21:44,745 --> 00:21:47,185
Comrade Ying, she’s quite capable.

317
00:21:47,425 --> 00:21:49,625
Train a bit more and once she's more comfortable,

318
00:21:49,625 --> 00:21:51,865
she can help ease Comrade Roong’s workload.

319
00:21:52,625 --> 00:21:54,425
Do you want to train Comrade Ying

320
00:21:54,425 --> 00:21:55,625
to replace Comrade Roong?

321
00:21:56,665 --> 00:22:01,145
Is this bad to add new talents in the base?

322
00:22:02,705 --> 00:22:05,065
Don’t think about who will replace whom;

323
00:22:05,065 --> 00:22:09,145
that kind of thinking won’t get us far.

324
00:22:12,785 --> 00:22:14,185
Do you get it?

325
00:22:19,145 --> 00:22:20,545
Yes, sir.

326
00:22:41,945 --> 00:22:43,345
Oh, Dan.

327
00:22:45,345 --> 00:22:46,745
Hello, Aunt La-or.

328
00:22:46,785 --> 00:22:48,625
What are you doing here?

329
00:22:48,745 --> 00:22:50,065
I just got around here,

330
00:22:50,105 --> 00:22:51,425
I thought I’d come pick you up.

331
00:22:51,425 --> 00:22:53,985
I also have something to talk to.

332
00:22:59,345 --> 00:23:02,505
Hey! Read it so you know what they’re up to.

333
00:23:02,505 --> 00:23:04,865
Our children won't become their tools.

334
00:23:04,905 --> 00:23:05,905
Rumor has it that...
Hanging with Communists is like holding a serpent.

335
00:23:05,905 --> 00:23:07,825
They brainwash people,
Hanging with Communists is like holding a serpent.

336
00:23:07,985 --> 00:23:08,825
telling them not to worship monks,

337
00:23:08,825 --> 00:23:10,065
not to respect their parents.

338
00:23:10,065 --> 00:23:10,905
Whoa!

339
00:23:11,545 --> 00:23:13,345
They say if you find those Red-Flag bastards,

340
00:23:13,345 --> 00:23:15,745
you can shoot them before asking.

341
00:23:17,625 --> 00:23:20,185
Hi, kid.

342
00:23:20,785 --> 00:23:22,345
You have to be very careful of them.

343
00:23:22,345 --> 00:23:23,385
Never trust a stranger.

344
00:23:23,385 --> 00:23:25,025
Why don't they think that...

345
00:23:25,065 --> 00:23:27,825
the students who fled to the forest, are just an innocent.

346
00:23:28,825 --> 00:23:30,825
They are our children.

347
00:23:32,865 --> 00:23:34,865
I might disagree with Vin,

348
00:23:35,705 --> 00:23:39,025
but I believe that Vin is not what others say.

349
00:23:39,705 --> 00:23:41,385
Aunt La-or. I...

350
00:23:42,065 --> 00:23:45,105
I heard that Vin might be at the base in the northern region.

351
00:23:45,105 --> 00:23:47,465
I’m going to be on duty there.

352
00:23:48,905 --> 00:23:51,265
If I see him I'll definitely inform you.

353
00:23:54,785 --> 00:23:56,345
Thank you so much, Dan.

354
00:23:59,625 --> 00:24:04,425
Dan, I want to give him something through you.

355
00:24:07,425 --> 00:24:09,025
No problem, Aunt La-or.

356
00:24:11,505 --> 00:24:12,865
Thank you.

357
00:24:13,305 --> 00:24:14,665
You're welcome.

358
00:24:20,625 --> 00:24:22,465
Stealth movement

359
00:24:22,465 --> 00:24:24,025
training means moving as quietly as possible

360
00:24:24,465 --> 00:24:25,585
on the battlefield.

361
00:24:26,225 --> 00:24:28,105
The moment the enemy knows our spot,

362
00:24:29,825 --> 00:24:32,785
we turn from hunters into the hunted.

363
00:24:35,385 --> 00:24:37,705
Wherever I hear the sound,

364
00:24:38,585 --> 00:24:39,265
Ouch!

365
00:24:40,025 --> 00:24:40,665
Ouch!

366
00:24:44,785 --> 00:24:46,025
I'll shoot.

367
00:24:48,225 --> 00:24:51,945
If I hear any movement from you next time, I won't aim at your body,

368
00:24:51,945 --> 00:24:53,945
but straight at the forehead.

369
00:24:57,345 --> 00:24:57,985
Ouch!

370
00:25:02,465 --> 00:25:04,225
Whoever reaches the big tree first

371
00:25:04,425 --> 00:25:05,425
will receive the reward from me.

372
00:25:39,465 --> 00:25:40,145
Whoa!

373
00:25:54,665 --> 00:25:55,305
What's wrong with you?

374
00:26:06,825 --> 00:26:08,185
I reach it in first place.

375
00:26:08,705 --> 00:26:10,025
Where's my reward?

376
00:26:13,705 --> 00:26:15,025
Do you have it?

377
00:26:26,345 --> 00:26:27,705
A banana?

378
00:26:28,585 --> 00:26:30,505
I run for a mile, just to get a banana?

379
00:26:31,345 --> 00:26:32,105
That's the reward.

380
00:26:32,705 --> 00:26:33,425
A reward?

381
00:26:33,905 --> 00:26:35,745
Eat it. You'll gain more strength to run.

382
00:26:37,905 --> 00:26:38,625
Comrade!

383
00:26:41,065 --> 00:26:43,385
I’ve seen Thai soldiers patrolling nearby.

384
00:26:48,145 --> 00:26:49,545
Take everyone back to the base.

385
00:26:49,545 --> 00:26:50,745
I'll check on it.

386
00:26:50,745 --> 00:26:51,545
I'll go with you.

387
00:26:51,545 --> 00:26:52,945
No, you won't

388
00:26:53,905 --> 00:26:55,225
The rest of you follow me.

389
00:26:56,585 --> 00:26:57,905
Go.

390
00:27:07,705 --> 00:27:08,985
Why do you follow me?

391
00:27:09,025 --> 00:27:10,345
Go back to the base.

392
00:27:10,705 --> 00:27:11,265
But...

393
00:27:11,265 --> 00:27:12,065
This is the command.

394
00:28:03,945 --> 00:28:05,305
You arrive late than I thought.

395
00:28:05,905 --> 00:28:06,825
Oh!

396
00:28:07,425 --> 00:28:08,305
How did you get here before us?

397
00:28:09,305 --> 00:28:11,985
What about the Thai soldiers?

398
00:28:13,785 --> 00:28:15,705
The soldier can't intrude on our base.

399
00:28:16,985 --> 00:28:19,785
Actually, another comrade is practicing shooting.

400
00:28:24,625 --> 00:28:25,705
This is just a test.

401
00:28:25,705 --> 00:28:28,985
In a real situation, whoever panics will die.

402
00:28:34,825 --> 00:28:36,305
Where's Comrade Saeng?

403
00:28:36,585 --> 00:28:37,865
Well...

404
00:28:38,465 --> 00:28:39,505
Where is he?

405
00:28:44,625 --> 00:28:47,265
You two, head to the stream we just left.

406
00:28:47,265 --> 00:28:49,865
Both of you, search at the yard where we had practiced.

407
00:28:49,865 --> 00:28:51,265
I'll search along the path.

408
00:28:56,745 --> 00:28:58,145
Comrade Yue!

409
00:29:01,305 --> 00:29:02,705
Comrade Yue!

410
00:29:05,785 --> 00:29:07,185
Comrade Yue!

411
00:29:18,785 --> 00:29:21,305
Comrade Yue!

412
00:29:21,745 --> 00:29:23,345
Comrade Yue!

413
00:29:24,385 --> 00:29:26,025
Comrade Yue!

414
00:29:44,865 --> 00:29:46,505
Comrade Yue!

415
00:30:06,185 --> 00:30:07,825
Help me.

416
00:30:10,905 --> 00:30:12,545
Arghhhhhh!!!!

417
00:30:20,905 --> 00:30:22,105
Comrade Saeng!

418
00:30:24,665 --> 00:30:25,705
Comrade Saeng!

419
00:30:36,345 --> 00:30:37,545
Comrade Saeng!

420
00:30:58,025 --> 00:30:59,225
Comrade Saeng!

421
00:31:04,665 --> 00:31:05,865
Comrade Saeng!

422
00:31:10,105 --> 00:31:11,305
Comrade Saeng!

423
00:31:18,465 --> 00:31:19,665
It's me. Comrade Saeng.

424
00:31:24,265 --> 00:31:25,465
Comrade Saeng.

425
00:31:33,465 --> 00:31:34,665
It's me.

426
00:31:45,985 --> 00:31:47,185
Comrade Yue!

427
00:31:49,025 --> 00:31:50,225
Where have you been?

428
00:31:50,905 --> 00:31:52,105
I’ve been trying to find you.

429
00:31:55,825 --> 00:31:57,025
It's OK, Comrade Saeng.

430
00:32:16,425 --> 00:32:19,345
If I'm here, you'll be fine.

431
00:32:29,585 --> 00:32:30,825
Go back to the base.

432
00:32:47,185 --> 00:32:48,185
Get on my back.

433
00:32:48,225 --> 00:32:49,225
Get on your back?

434
00:32:49,225 --> 00:32:50,225
Get on my back

435
00:33:18,625 --> 00:33:21,305
This area is all Hmong villages.

436
00:33:21,545 --> 00:33:22,465
Where are you going?

437
00:33:22,465 --> 00:33:23,425
Gather some forest stuff.

438
00:33:23,545 --> 00:33:24,505
I see.

439
00:33:25,545 --> 00:33:26,505
Good luck!

440
00:33:27,865 --> 00:33:30,825
The path to the left leads up the mountain.

441
00:33:30,825 --> 00:33:33,065
And the right leads to the stream.

442
00:33:33,065 --> 00:33:37,425
As for this route.. that side uses it to transport supplies.

443
00:33:39,305 --> 00:33:40,105
Supplies?

444
00:33:43,585 --> 00:33:44,385
Shi Wang

445
00:33:47,905 --> 00:33:48,505
Ma'am.

446
00:33:50,465 --> 00:33:51,185
Do you know where she lives?

447
00:33:51,225 --> 00:33:51,945
Yes, I do.

448
00:33:53,585 --> 00:33:55,225
Do you want me to send more rice, elder?

449
00:33:55,705 --> 00:33:58,025
My family barely has enough to eat as it is.

450
00:33:58,025 --> 00:34:00,785
Whether you have it or not, that's not my damn business!

451
00:34:01,145 --> 00:34:04,225
If you don't want trouble, then do as I say.

452
00:34:05,145 --> 00:34:07,825
Please, I beg of you, Please help me!

453
00:34:07,825 --> 00:34:09,945
Yaguar.. Yaguar.. Your mother fainted!

454
00:34:10,865 --> 00:34:12,785
Mother! Mother!

455
00:34:13,745 --> 00:34:14,665
Let's go inside first.

456
00:34:14,665 --> 00:34:15,665
Mother!

457
00:34:18,145 --> 00:34:19,825
Your mother fainted. Luckily,

458
00:34:19,825 --> 00:34:21,825
this gentleman helped her just in time.

459
00:34:25,505 --> 00:34:27,785
Thank you so much for saving my mother.

460
00:34:29,425 --> 00:34:30,705
But.. who are you?

461
00:34:30,705 --> 00:34:32,185
I've never seen your face around here before.

462
00:34:34,025 --> 00:34:35,425
He’s from Bangkok.

463
00:34:35,665 --> 00:34:37,825
He’s here looking for land to grow vegetables for sale.

464
00:34:40,825 --> 00:34:42,265
Thank you again.

465
00:34:43,945 --> 00:34:47,505
We should head back now. Let your mother get some rest.

466
00:34:55,065 --> 00:34:56,545
If she doesn’t get any better,

467
00:34:56,545 --> 00:34:58,105
have Yang Sue come and tell me.

468
00:34:59,785 --> 00:35:02,985
Thank you, sir. You’re a truly good man.

469
00:35:05,425 --> 00:35:09,025
Was there trouble earlier? Things looked a bit tense.

470
00:35:17,505 --> 00:35:21,665
It’s about the rice. This field I’m farming... it’s not mine.

471
00:35:23,625 --> 00:35:25,625
I have to give a portion to the landlord,

472
00:35:25,625 --> 00:35:27,665
and another to the village chief.

473
00:35:28,305 --> 00:35:31,865
Whatever’s left is all we have to eat.

474
00:35:38,025 --> 00:35:39,625
Sometimes I don't understand.

475
00:35:40,625 --> 00:35:43,385
My mother and I work ourselves to death in the rice fields.

476
00:35:45,465 --> 00:35:47,945
But we only get to eat rice a little.

477
00:35:50,905 --> 00:35:54,625
That's how it is. We have no rights, no voice.

478
00:36:03,545 --> 00:36:06,985
I’ve heard how hard it is for the people here.

479
00:36:10,385 --> 00:36:13,105
But seeing it for myself.. it’s no surprise,

480
00:36:14,905 --> 00:36:17,025
why some people choose other path.

481
00:36:21,305 --> 00:36:25,225
Anyway, thank you again for helping my mother today.

482
00:36:27,145 --> 00:36:28,505
Go check on her.

483
00:36:33,025 --> 00:36:34,385
Go on.

484
00:36:46,385 --> 00:36:47,745
Feel better?

485
00:36:52,505 --> 00:36:53,865
You should wash your face to feel refreshed.

486
00:37:14,305 --> 00:37:15,985
Why did you get so scared?

487
00:37:37,145 --> 00:37:39,185
While I was running in the forest,

488
00:37:43,145 --> 00:37:44,585
I heard the sound of the bomb.

489
00:37:47,105 --> 00:37:48,905
It brought back memories of that day at the university.

490
00:37:52,065 --> 00:37:54,505
My friend was killed by the bomb right in front of me.

491
00:38:05,505 --> 00:38:07,305
Haven't you forgotten what happened at the university?

492
00:38:16,545 --> 00:38:18,705
I feel guilty that my friend was killed,

493
00:38:20,665 --> 00:38:22,705
and I still feel guilty for surviving.

494
00:38:41,025 --> 00:38:42,825
You know, it's not your fault.

495
00:38:51,585 --> 00:38:53,105
I get how you feel.

496
00:38:53,905 --> 00:38:55,585
No one can escape the guilt.

497
00:39:01,225 --> 00:39:02,705
Just keep holding on,

498
00:39:06,865 --> 00:39:08,345
and speak for your friend.

499
00:39:10,105 --> 00:39:11,465
Do it for him,

500
00:39:14,225 --> 00:39:16,065
the thing he’ll never get a chance to do.

501
00:39:33,025 --> 00:39:34,865
Why do you smoke?

502
00:39:39,625 --> 00:39:41,265
Do you have anything on your mind?

503
00:39:46,665 --> 00:39:49,425
It's OK if you don’t want to share, I’m just asking.

504
00:39:56,785 --> 00:39:58,305
I saw the people I love,

505
00:39:59,985 --> 00:40:01,745
all of my comrades,

506
00:40:03,705 --> 00:40:05,105
die right in front of me.

507
00:40:10,185 --> 00:40:11,945
It happened everyday until it became normal.

508
00:40:14,305 --> 00:40:15,385
I don't know yet,

509
00:40:15,385 --> 00:40:16,505
when it'll be my turn.

510
00:40:26,305 --> 00:40:27,385
This smoke...

511
00:40:27,385 --> 00:40:29,945
is like a reminder that I'm still alive.

512
00:40:42,505 --> 00:40:46,065
I guess.. it's just an excuse to make yourself look cool.

513
00:40:47,265 --> 00:40:48,665
Am I right?

514
00:40:59,905 --> 00:41:01,345
So, Am I cool?

515
00:41:07,345 --> 00:41:08,185
Um.

516
00:41:25,945 --> 00:41:28,385
They live hand-to-mouth here

517
00:41:28,385 --> 00:41:29,705
because they don't have money.

518
00:41:29,705 --> 00:41:31,985
Most of them forage for food in the forests and mountains.

519
00:41:33,105 --> 00:41:34,945
How many families live here?

520
00:41:36,105 --> 00:41:39,785
I didn't count them, but there were probably several dozen.

521
00:41:52,625 --> 00:41:54,105
Ask anything you want.

522
00:41:54,945 --> 00:41:57,105
Why did you bring us on a trip today?

523
00:42:00,785 --> 00:42:02,025
Who said we’re on a trip?

524
00:42:02,785 --> 00:42:04,345
Comrade Ploeng trusts you

525
00:42:04,345 --> 00:42:06,985
to reach out to the masses. We’re here to work.

526
00:42:07,265 --> 00:42:09,105
I know. Just kidding.

527
00:42:09,545 --> 00:42:11,505
Our job is to invite as many people as possible to join.

528
00:42:11,505 --> 00:42:14,145
The more people you win over, the faster you'll win.

529
00:42:15,385 --> 00:42:17,465
To get someone to join us,

530
00:42:17,745 --> 00:42:19,265
you must learn to give first.

531
00:42:19,585 --> 00:42:22,385
Just wander in, who's going to join with you?

532
00:42:22,705 --> 00:42:24,025
Give?

533
00:42:24,065 --> 00:42:26,185
We don't even have enough meat to eat ourselves,

534
00:42:26,185 --> 00:42:27,065
so how can we give to anyone?

535
00:42:30,745 --> 00:42:34,225
Give what you can. Eat just enough, use just enough,

536
00:42:34,545 --> 00:42:35,825
The rest can be shared with others.

537
00:42:35,825 --> 00:42:37,825
If you have nothing, go help them out.

538
00:42:38,305 --> 00:42:41,305
It’s simple. Students like you should understand.

539
00:42:43,745 --> 00:42:45,385
Hey! Help!

540
00:42:48,065 --> 00:42:49,865
Help! Help my child!

541
00:42:51,545 --> 00:42:53,145
Help my child!

